// Pattern variables a closure captures are declared like any other local: the
// declaration puts the new value in the slot, replacing the cell of the
// previous iteration, so `UnpackLocals(1, 2)` covers them too, and there's no
// `Unpack`.
// compile: stdlib
fn f(xs: [(Int, Int)]) { for (a, b) in xs { fn() { a + b }; } }
